Boundary data
  Country outlines: johan/world.geo.json (Natural Earth 1:110m, public domain), /tmp/world.geo.json.
  tools/geo.py: Lambert azimuthal equal-area projection centred on each shape («истинный размер», one scale per comparison,
  1000 km scale bar shown), Douglas–Peucker simplification; Africa = union of its countries (shared borders cancelled);
  the phone map: Web-Mercator («веб-Меркатор»). tools/pack.py + tools/anneal.py: where the copies of France sit in DR Congo
  and the USA (contiguous + Alaska), China, India sit in Africa (moved and turned only; areas unchanged).
  The Moon's whole surface is drawn as an equal-area disc (radius 2 × 1737.4 km); the area squares use side = √area
  (Africa 30.07, Moon 37.9, Asia 44.58 million km²) at the same scale.
  Everything else drawn in marker. No generated images.

